Description: GHSA-h35g-vwh6-m678 (CVE-2024-8929, 2024) and the 2026 partial fix of GHSA-r6x9-5r99-36j7 for PHP 5.6: a hostile or man-in-the-middle MySQL server could make the mysqlnd client read past the end of a received packet and leak adjacent heap bytes into PHP-visible values, and in some paths free memory wrongly. 5.6 shipped neither fix (both are absent from Remi and Sury for 5.6), so both are carried over from PHP 7.4. php_mysqlnd_net_field_length() now takes the bytes left in the packet and returns MYSQLND_INVALID_NET_FIELD_LENGTH when a length-encoded integer would read past them; a new php_mysqlnd_net_field_length_ll() returns an optional value the callers must check. Every packet reader (greeting, auth response, OK, EOF, result-set header, column definition, prepare response, change-user, sha256 public key, and the text and binary row decoders) is bounded with BAIL_IF_NOT_ENOUGH_DATA_EX / explicit remaining-size checks, NUL-terminated strings are found with memchr instead of being assumed terminated, and the prepared-statement value decoders (ps_fetch_*) reject a declared length that runs past the row or is too short for the fixed type. A decode that fails frees or NULLs the already-decoded row zvals of 5.6 so the row can be freed safely, the BIT text value is bounded by the space reserved from the column length, read_result_metadata frees a failed result through free_result (not a bare efree that would leak the sub-objects), and the prepared-statement EOF reset releases the connection reference and command buffer before the memset. Tests use a new fake MySQL server (ext/mysqli/tests/fake_server.inc), adapted to PHP 5.6 syntax; the client handshake bytes that differ in 5.6 are matched with %s.
Origin: azsupport, port of php-src commits 2f5aa9f9d150 (GHSA-h35g-vwh6-m678 / CVE-2024-8929, Jakub Zelenka, 08.10.2024, PHP-8.1) and 2af14de0f223 (Partial Fix GHSA-r6x9-5r99-36j7, Jakub Zelenka and Nora Dossche, 12.07.2026) of the PHP 7.4 security branch of Remi Collet (remicollet/php-src-security PHP-7.4-security-backports)

